{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1227902-how-do-groups-handle-mind-control","id":1227902,"title":"How do groups handle Mind control?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-16T14:34:38-07:00","id":1227902,"title":"How do groups handle Mind control?","content":"Vampires, Werewolves' mages, changelings, hunter's how do they respond to one of their own having been mind bended?<br /> <br /> The last most of all as I think witnessing such powers is all the more terrifying to those without them oneself<br /> <br /> Just think what its like for an SAD Agent or DNA/Pentex/Belpharoon Foundation employee to be held at gunpoint by a friend and comrade?<br /> <br /> Can you <b>know </b>beyond all doubt your friend isnt programmed to do it again?<br /> <br /> How do you know <b>your </b>not?<br /> <br /> garou I think may be contempuous to another Garou who commits treason because of mystical compulsion but wont kill him just sneer at him because of his weakness of will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-17-2018, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T16:12:48-07:00","id":1228701,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Dominate&quot; discipline that vampires have is very frustrating for my pack of werewolves, but that's largely because the storyteller's NPC leeches have had very lucky rolls <i>every</i> time they've tried it. It's not so much a horrifying thing to be afraid of, but it pisses the werewolves off when it allows the leeches to escape. The more formidable kinds of mind control, like the higher levels of vampiric &quot;Presence&quot; or whatever mind control or illusion a mage might cook up, would be more disturbing. I'd guess that werewolves would probably be able to cope with it psychologically much more easily than creatures who don't have personal experience with the stranger things happening in the spirit world, and the more &quot;normal&quot; human types, like hunters or human Pentex employees, would have a very hard time coping. The most frightening kinds of mind control would certainly be those with a time-delayed trigger, like what happens with Reggie Jackson in the Naked Gun. I'm not sure how any victim (the used or the targeted) could handle that, but if the person who inflicted the mind control it was identified, they'd have to be marked as enemy number one and put at the top of the list of people who need to be killed ASAP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","user":"Wilson","date":". 06-19-2018, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T06:48:15-07:00","id":1229141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1227902-how-do-groups-handle-mind-control#post1227902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires, Werewolves' mages, changelings, hunter's how do they respond to one of their own having been mind bended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages getting co-opted by force and turned against their former friends it's far from unheard off. The life of a Tradition mage in the middle of the Ascension War it's to know that at any time your friends and lovers may get captured by the Technocracy and be mindrapped in room 101. At the same time, Traditionalists aren't always above using mind control themselves.<br /> This does generate a state of paranoia where checking the soul and mind of members it's seen as a common practice - which it's by no means foolproof, as magick can frustrate such perceptions. Technocrats answer the problem by having their members submit regularly to mind reading and mind control to reinforce their loyalty - which also isn't foolproof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-21-2018, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T19:42:34-07:00","id":1229278,"title":"","content":"how do you think a dancer pack would react to a packmate who turned against them because of &quot;The Hateful Silver Fang the Accursed Gaian! I swear I am still loyal to our Father!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> because of the <i>Mastery </i>Gift,, especialy if he killed one of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T12:08:31-07:00","id":1229426,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, getting mindrapped it's going to be a blow to the controled packmate's Renown...That you were controled proves your mind it's WEAK!. If she killed one of them, well, she demonstrated certain kind of strength by achieving that but still acted against the Wyrm's Chosen, that's no good. <br /> <br /> After that, well, it depends. She surely will try/have to retaliate (more Power to her if she does so without help, but fortunately that's not the only Renown Trait). Achieving this would prove her loyalty to the Wyrm and recover lost Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T14:04:30-07:00","id":1229451,"title":"","content":"Think dancer's would be capable of Grief or guilt for the death of a friend? <br /> <br /> <br /> ideas how SAD Society of leopold or other hunter organizations will react?<br /> <br /> wondering if SAD has a section on how to handle such cases in their manuals or even a manual totally about how to respond to mind control.<br /> <br /> It would be very disturbing to a hunter who does not have access to similar magics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T16:50:54-07:00","id":1230126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1227902-how-do-groups-handle-mind-control?p=1229451#post1229451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think dancers would be capable of Grief or guilt for the death of a friend?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dancing the Black Spiral is a mindrape in itself, but the BSDs end up embracing the Wyrm instead of being reduced to puppets or zombies, so I figure they still have their instincts for pack loyalty, pride in their devotion to a common cause, etc., that would give them reason to regret the loss of a packmate. I could be wrong, but I figure the natural emotions they're born with are corrupted rather than destroyed, so grief and guilt could still exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T17:26:26-07:00","id":1230131,"title":"","content":"something tell's me the dancer's would not go to extraordinary lenghts to capture a fellow who fell to <i>Obedience </i>unhurt, even though some who Follow Hakkaken the Heart of fear probaly seek the gift out.<br /> <br /> on <i>Obedience</i>, what Could a Gaian ask of a Dancer with 1-4 successes, or vice versa in afore mentioned case?<br /> <br /> <br /> Was wondering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T16:26:53-07:00","id":1230394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1227902-how-do-groups-handle-mind-control?p=1230131#post1230131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on <i>Obedience</i>, what Could a Gaian ask of a Dancer with 1-4 successes, or vice versa in afore mentioned case?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read on wrymfoe.com, at 3 successes the targets treat you as their alpha, so essentially they're loyal to you and will take orders from you while the effects last. For a werewolf, whether Gaian or BSD, I figure that would mean the targets would be willing to do whatever they'd normally be willing to do for their own pack's alpha, and at 4 successes they might take serious risks for the sake of their &quot;alpha&quot; though even at 5 successes it's qualified as &quot;near suicidal.&quot; So &quot;kill yourself&quot; isn't going to work, but orders to fight with or for you likely would, depending on how crazy or risky the orders are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T05:17:13-07:00","id":1230771,"title":"","content":"thing is, obeying an <b>enemy </b>even to answer questions is near suicidal.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do you think Hunter organizations such as the SAD, Illuminati, Society of Leopold, the Imbued or DNA will react to mind control<br /> <br /> I could see DNA Wanting to do neural tests on someone who was mind controlled by a Garou, because &quot;Their Must be a rational explanation for this!!!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-28-2018, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T20:22:36-07:00","id":1233896,"title":"","content":"oh something I was thinking on? <br /> <br /> Think SAD or DNA In particular, maybe illuminati since they want to know everything<br /> <br /> <br /> would want to do CAT Scans or such on someone they knew to have recently been effected with mind controlling magic to try deducing just WTF it is<br /> <br /> SAD would be desperately scrambling for countermeasures and outraged to find theirs none, at least none they can find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"imag